encies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.5.stable.official [876b29033]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti SUPER (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7680) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900K (32 threads) - 31.76 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nGodot crashes when using autocomplete (TAB) on a concrete method wanting to override an abstract method from an abstract class that contains both the abstract method and a separate concrete methos inside of it with a doc comment.\n\nThings I've tested:\n1. The concrete method has to have a doc comment\n2. The abstract method having a doc comment or not does not seem to affect behaviour\n3. Without the doc comment everything works as expected and there is no crash\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create an abstract class with an abstract method and a concrete method <img width=\"964\" height=\"673\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b510f9c6-b0ec-4496-89ad-1237db9013e8\" />\n2. Add a doc comment to the concrete method\n3. Create a concrete class that extends this \n4. Type in `func` + the abstract function name until autocomplete suggests it <---- The wrong comment is also picked up by the editor preview here <img width=\"1459\" height=\"717\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d61c299c-bb4c-4476-8dbb-19b8b495e054\" />\n\n5. Press TAB <--- Godot crashes here \n\nAs a comment, I would be happy to contribute a fix with some guidance :).\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22432616/MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","follo